        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/839c29/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-05-26T02:03:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"jffdougan\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jffdougan/48/1882_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jffdougan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>morph147 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I will add that if GTG wanted to make some money, an insert system for this game that can hold everything to date can be huge.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nit's definitely an option in Broken Token's poll, and there's a guy who does a foamcore insert that holds everything but uses both boxes, and I've seen at least one set of plans on BGG for a laser cutter. the interest is definitely there.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Ya I learned today the guy who did the laser cutter is one of my coworkers. I havent given up on the 3D print idea but either A) the printer keeps failing that is large enough to do what I want to do or B) the smaller printer works but the bottom warps which causes it not to be as functional.</p>",
